{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/klopezva/.claude/skills/coord\n\n# Filesystem Coordination\n\n1. Run the `coord_status` MCP tool (or `coord-status.sh <project>`) before\n   nontrivial work in this repo. `project` is the absolute path to the repo root.\n2. Follow `coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`. Post a `claim` via `coord_post` with\n   concrete files/sections BEFORE editing; respect the edit budget in\n   `coord/OPERATING_MODE.md`; never start silently.\n3. Reviews: `[blocker]` / `[suggestion]` / `[nit]`; respond accepted /\n   rejected-because / deferred.\n4. Escalate principal-only decisions with `coord_escalate` (or by editing\n   `coord/HUMAN.md` directly if MCP is unavailable).\n5. If another agent is needed and stale, post `type: stale-ping` addressed to\n   it; `coord-pulse.sh --agent <name>` handles wake-up.\n6. Do NOT spawn Agent Teams to do work that another vendor's agent has\n   claimed in `coord/threads/`. If the principal asks for a Codex/agy\n   consult, post a thread message addressed to that agent and let\n   `coord-pulse.sh` wake them — don't spawn a subagent named after them.\n7. If `coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md` is missing, offer to run the kit's\n   `bootstrap.sh`; do not invent a protocol.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: wake manual T-006 segunda vuelta: fichas por pregunta de investigación + gaps"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c941fff-a85c-417c-ae34-d68a383e6ff3","uuid":"ebe6561d-88c8-46aa-b578-2fa4833be78d","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:19:46.412Z","isSynthetic":true}
